# dartwork-mpl

Plotting rules live in one place, the skill bundled with the package:
`src/dartwork_mpl/skills/dartwork-mpl/SKILL.md` and its `references/`.
Read it before writing or reviewing plot code. Contributor rules (design
documents, the colour freeze, MCP freeze) are in `AGENTS.md`.

The short version:

- `dm.style.use(preset)` first: `scientific` paper, `report` documents,
  `presentation` slides; `-kr` only for Korean plot text.
- `plt.subplots(figsize=dm.figsize("13cm", "standard"))`; never
  `figsize=(w, h)` or `dpi=` on figure creation.
- `dm.simple_layout(fig)` after drawing; never `plt.tight_layout()`.
- `dm.save_formats(fig, "output/name", formats=("png", "pdf"))`, then open the
  PNG and read `dm.validate_figure(fig, quiet=True)`.
- Edit only the requested target; keep data, preset, size and style.

Code in this repository: runtime dependencies with `uv add`, tools with
`uv add --dev`; NumPy-style docstrings; Python 3.10+ type hints on every
function (`uv run mypy` is strict); `uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff
format .` before committing; no stray render outputs in commits.
